# This file is the switch, not a setting: /etc/init.d/S00bootlog only checks
# whether it exists. Its presence raises the console to printk level 8 at boot,
# which adds KERN_DEBUG to what the kernel was already printing.
#
# Shipped present because this image is meant to be read while it boots. The
# kernel command line deliberately carries no `quiet` (patches 0049 and 0060),
# so the boot streams live at CONFIG_CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_DEFAULT=7 and nothing has
# to be replayed. `bootlog quiet` removes this file and drops the console to
# level 4. It survives reboots in the persistent /etc jffs2 partition.
